on this Mother's Day there's lots of  virtual hugging going on everyone is  longing for the day when we can get  close again for those women who are  pregnant right now motherhood is about  to get very real babies of course don't  wait around for a crisis to subside what  is it like to be expecting in the midst  of all of this  well we're following a couple who are  due to have their first baby in just a  few days they've been documenting their  journey of what to expect when you are  expecting during a pandemic I'm Kareem  and I'm Eli and we're having a baby and  the time of coronavirus it's true we met  four years ago while I was at Vancouver  for work I was living in Toronto she was  living in Vancouver so he did the  long-distance thing for a while bouncing  back and forth between the two cities a  big part of our lives and a relationship  is travelling and adventures whether  it's camping interesti exploring new  countries or just going for a hike we  love getting outside and trying new  things  so when we found out last fall we were  pregnant we were pretty pumped to embark  on this new adventure we were in Ontario  at the time and things started off  fairly normal doctor's visits this is  what you look like in 19 weeks  hanging out with friends and family we  headed back west in January we even went  on a babymoon to Palm Springs toured  around on bikes elephant cruiser bikes  not so easy green killing it up there  she's biking for to exploit Joshua Tree  clownish in the pools life was good but  after we got back things started to  change pretty quickly the reality is  that the number of people affected by  the virus around the globe keeps  climbing coronavirus was becoming more  of a thing and people were starting to  talk about it it started with little  things like no more high-fives of  volleyball then an environmental  conference I was to attend in Vegas got  canceled and the next thing you know  things started shutting down I was  really excited for my sister to come  visit in March but we had to cancel her  trip questions started being raised  about our health care options as we  entered the third trimester and our  day-to-day shifted as everyone started  isolating can we go to the hospital is  the hospital even safe if we get sick  the baby get Kovac and my mom still what  does this mean financially how long is  this going to lie or do we go from here  there are a lot of questions and to most  the answer was unknown it doesn't stress  you out that I can't come to the  appointments in person no the first time  definitely was a little bit more intense  because it was our first appointment  during coal bed so the midwives were  wearing masks there's no one else in the  waiting room it just had a totally  different feel but now that we've done  it a few times and you can still  participate in call in and ask questions  and hear our updates it's okay so like  everyone we had to trust in the experts  stay at home and focus on what we can  control  like makeshift grocery masks I don't  have a real mask so I'm using my ski  mask to cover my face just as an attempt  to make it a little bit safer I got my  hand sanitizer I got my lifestyle wipes  the reality is we're 39 weeks in and if  I get kovin now I won't be able to be  there for the birth of my child which  would suck so ski masks up let's get  some pampers  and watching everything that came in the  house just in case could be nice  analyzed enough we wrote our birth wish  list it'd be nice to be in a hospital  birth to be able to come back input yeah  in order to pull it we installed the car  seat dad life we tried to stay active  with workouts and going to the beach our  social life moved online we took her own  maternity folders I started wrapping up  work and we join an online group with  other expecting parents we took a baby  class online and I joined our Midwife  appointments from my phone through it  all we were blessed with love and  support from friends and family they  kept us grounded and helped us celebrate  this new chapter a friend made us a  quilt my cousin's staff made us a mobile  and loved one spoiled us with  hand-me-downs and thoughtful gifts they  even planned a surprise shower over zoo  I heard someone say the other day we're  all on the same storm but we're in  different boats but I think that is so  true we've been blessed with a healthy  pregnancy and because we are in DC at  the moment our birth options are pretty  stable we could still have our midwives  and our doula and I can still attend the  birth but for many that's not the case  everybody's situation is different and  everyone handles things differently this  isn't really what I pictured for the  our pregnancy there have been  disappointments and tears but at the end  of the day we are okay and we have so  much to be grateful for we don't know  what the future holds  especially during this pandemic things  could go totally sideways at a moment's  notice but for now we're just gonna try  and make the most of things soak it all  in because this baby will be here before  we know it  [Music]
 

